================================================================================
Known third-party license edge cases
================================================================================

  - @codesandbox/nodebox is present in the dependency tree as a transitive
    of @mdxeditor/editor → @codesandbox/sandpack-react →
    @codesandbox/sandpack-client → nodebox. It is distributed under the
    Sustainable Use License (SUL), a source-available non-OSI license whose
    redistribution terms are stricter than AGPL-3.0.

    Status (audited 2026-05-02): MnM does NOT import any Sandpack plugin
    anywhere in its source code. The MarkdownEditor uses CodeMirror plugins
    only (codeBlockPlugin + codeMirrorPlugin). As a result, Vite's
    tree-shaking eliminates the Sandpack subgraph — including
    @codesandbox/nodebox — from the production bundle that is actually
    distributed to end users.

    Conclusion: the SUL/AGPL boundary is not crossed by the distributed
    artifacts. The dependency remains in node_modules during development
    (a build-time concern), but is not part of the AGPL-licensed Work that
    ships to users. Documented here for transparency and to flag any future
    change (e.g. enabling the Sandpack code preview plugin) that would
    re-introduce the question and require dropping the dependency or
    vendoring an OSI-compatible alternative.
